{
  "arguments": {
    "query": "vLLM Automatic Prefix Caching what is cached reuse conditions"
  },
  "observation": {
    "evidence": [
      {
        "id": "E95f5d58c5d1ad9b20f4e6963",
        "chunk_id": "a08ce15828b4c5715fa914f7",
        "parent_id": "e2f783bc52fc6d11dba52420",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L3-L13",
        "content": "Prefix caching kv-cache blocks is a popular optimization in LLM inference to avoid redundant prompt computations.\nThe core idea is simple – we cache the kv-cache blocks of processed requests, and reuse these blocks when a new request comes in with the same prefix as previous requests.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E620d3ddaad5ad2054c752d19",
        "chunk_id": "779175155be2b4c482fd5c25",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "To improve privacy in shared environments, vLLM supports isolating prefix cache reuse through optional per-request salting.\nBy including a `cache_salt` in the request, this value is injected into the hash of the first block, ensuring that only requests with the same salt can reuse cached KV blocks.\nThis prevents timing-based attacks where an adversary could infer cached content by observing latency differences.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E2e11ed500d592310a7422ca6",
        "chunk_id": "06a4698c9e4cb362ac120a20",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "With this setup, cache sharing is limited to users or requests that explicitly agree on a common salt, enabling cache reuse within a trust group while isolating others.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "Ee499d46e193d2a6f1f02191a",
        "chunk_id": "a27719ddbabb0b419d311028",
        "parent_id": "847202708939d2d1afa17774",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-automatic_prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "a939df40f6cde38cc48701cfee6626dbdc73c4f1e5df46921a7b88c496e31580",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-automatic_prefix_caching.md#L5-L5",
        "content": "Automatic Prefix Caching (APC in short) caches the KV cache of existing queries, so that a new query can directly reuse the KV cache if it shares the same prefix with one of the existing queries, allowing the new query to skip the computation of the shared part.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "Eb854405da807d8b3ab23555a",
        "chunk_id": "47996838d61718002c9543eb",
        "parent_id": "ecc41abf9035240b509f3b05",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-automatic_prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "a939df40f6cde38cc48701cfee6626dbdc73c4f1e5df46921a7b88c496e31580",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-automatic_prefix_caching.md#L20-L21",
        "content": "In this case, instead of processing the whole chatting history again and again, APC allows vLLM to reuse the processing results of the chat history across all future rounds of conversation, allowing vLLM to serve future requests with much higher throughput and much lower latency.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E8f67c161db19fd79595d505f",
        "chunk_id": "1b033b6229bf05e4e1b8f142",
        "parent_id": "e2f783bc52fc6d11dba52420",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L3-L13",
        "content": "Since prefix caching is almost a free lunch and won’t change model outputs, it has been widely used by many public endpoints (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, etc) and most open source LLM inference frameworks (e.g., SGLang).\nWhile there are many ways to implement prefix caching, vLLM chooses a hash-based approach.\nSpecifically, we hash each kv-cache block by the tokens in the block and the tokens in the prefix before the block:",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E11d41126bd9ee73aefd702d0",
        "chunk_id": "fa3be3ccc73460fcb8aa0935",
        "parent_id": "e2f783bc52fc6d11dba52420",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L3-L13",
        "content": "```text\n                    Block 1                  Block 2                  Block 3\n         [A gentle breeze stirred] [the leaves as children] [laughed in the distance]\nBlock 1: |<--- block tokens ---->|\nBlock 2: |<------- prefix ------>| |<--- block tokens --->|\nBlock 3: |<------------------ prefix -------------------->| |<--- block tokens ---->|\n```",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E18df8d7de69a9bc239731abf",
        "chunk_id": "28bc81fe7e8f333b5d5c57d9",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "In the rest of this document, we first introduce the data structure used for prefix caching in vLLM v1, followed by the prefix caching workflow of major KV cache operators (e.g., allocate, append, free, eviction).\nFinally, we use an example to illustrate the end to end prefix caching workflow.\n**Cache Isolation for Security**",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E1c5b7341c4d64d891d9a1cfe",
        "chunk_id": "7c1a6df7e7a23c7671ff1794",
        "parent_id": "a246f31f42c4cc1a08a38919",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "0a8a9e9095055c4f8e0cdaf078e3194ab06428222d65abb9c827f6879607ce61",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-prefix_caching.md#L79-L98",
        "content": "!!\n! note\nCache isolation is not supported in engine V0.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E4276ce8267fe0abe2148605b",
        "chunk_id": "39592a76e1a8ae9f68fee0b0",
        "parent_id": "ecc41abf9035240b509f3b05",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-automatic_prefix_caching.md",
        "sha256": "a939df40f6cde38cc48701cfee6626dbdc73c4f1e5df46921a7b88c496e31580",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-automatic_prefix_caching.md#L20-L21",
        "content": "This allows vLLM to serve future requests with much higher throughput and much lower latency.\n- Multi-round conversation, where the user may chat with the application multiple times in the same chatting session.",
        "truncated": false,
